invariant: INV-9
file: record.c
catches: aes_suite_test
reason: rec_seal copies one byte less than the caller's plaintext into the
  record, so the last byte of every record is whatever the output buffer
  held before, sealed and authenticated as if the caller had written it.
  The copy is one memmove, which gcc runs as the C library's vector copy
  where it ran the byte loop before it; bin/aes_suite_test seals RFC
  8448's AES-128-GCM record and the Illustrated TLS 1.3 AES-256-GCM one
  through rec_seal and compares the record with the published bytes.

--- old
    memmove(inner, pt, n);
--- new
    memmove(inner, pt, n - (n > 0));
